# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form email delivery (OPTIONAL).
# Without these, the contact form gracefully falls back to a prefilled mailto:
# link, so the site works with zero configuration.
#
# To enable real email delivery (submits a real inquiry + auto-reply to the
# visitor confirming receipt):
#   1. Create a free account at https://resend.com
#   2. Create an API key (Settings → API Keys) and set RESEND_API_KEY below.
#      At this point CONTACT_TO_EMAIL will work if it's the SAME address you
#      signed up to Resend with (their sandbox sender can only deliver to
#      your own account email until a domain is verified).
#   3. To also auto-reply to VISITORS (arbitrary email addresses, not just
#      your own), add & verify a domain you own under Domains, then set
#      CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL to an address on that domain (e.g.
#      hello@yourdomain.com). Without a verified domain, the auto-reply
#      silently no-ops — the inquiry to CONTACT_TO_EMAIL still goes through.
#   4. Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Resend API key (server-only, never exposed to the client).
RESEND_API_KEY=

# The address the contact form sends to (your inbox).
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=akashmadduru@gmail.com

# The verified "from" address on your Resend domain.
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=onboarding@resend.dev

# Public canonical site URL (used for SEO metadata, sitemap, OG images).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://akashmadduru.dev
